# UI Toolkit First (New UI)

From here forward, **all new player-facing UI** is built with **UI Toolkit** — not uGUI (`Canvas`, `Image`, `TextMeshProUGUI`, `MenuUiBuilder` runtime panels).

## Required stack

| Layer | Location / pattern |
|-------|-------------------|
| Layout | `Assets/UI Toolkit/Screens/<Screen>.uxml` |
| Styles | Screen `.uss` + `Assets/UI Toolkit/Themes/DarkMatterGenesis.uss` |
| Runtime | `Assets/UI Toolkit/Runtime/DMUiToolkit*.cs` (`MonoBehaviour` on a named `UIDocument` host) |
| Colors | `DarkMatterGenesisUiPalette` / Shift theme (`dark-matter-genesis-ui-palette.mdc`) |
| Naming | `DM` / `DMI` prefixes for new project UI types (`dm-naming-no-invector.mdc`) |

## Host documents (reuse — do not invent a second HUD root)

- **Gameplay HUD / journal chrome:** `UITK_Hud` (`DMUiToolkitHud`, `DMUiToolkitMenus`)
- **Main menu / pause modals:** `UITK_MainMenu`, `DMUiToolkitMenuPanels` siblings
- **Fullscreen overlays:** `DMUiToolkitOverlayDocument.Ensure(...)` (optics, loading, etc.)
- **Panel settings:** share bootstrap `PanelSettings` via `DMUiToolkitBootstrap`

## Do

- Add UXML elements with stable `name=` ids; bind in C# with `root.Q<T>(...)`.
- Use USS classes (`dmg-*`) for layout and state — avoid inline styles except dynamic values.
- Wire input through existing bridges (`DMUiToolkitInputHost`, `GameplayKeyboardShortcuts`, Input System).
- Disable or hide legacy uGUI for the same surface when UITK drives it (`DMUiToolkitUguiRetirement` pattern).

## Do not

- Create new `Canvas` menu/HUD/popup hierarchies with `MenuUiBuilder`, TMP labels, or `GraphicRaycaster` stacks.
- Add new uGUI “fallback” panels “just in case” when `DMUiToolkitConfig.IsEnabled` — ship UITK only.
- Expand retired surfaces (wallet, legacy MainCanvas chrome) in uGUI.

## Legacy uGUI

Existing uGUI under `MainCanvas` / Invector may remain until deliberately migrated. When **touching** a UI feature for new work, **extend or replace with UITK** — do not add parallel uGUI.

## Exceptions

Only build uGUI when the user **explicitly** requests legacy uGUI for that task, or the target is third-party package UI that cannot be UITK-wrapped yet (document why in the PR/commit note).
